40018</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bao</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Cui</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Prediction of the phenotypic effects of non-synonymous single nucleotide polymorphisms using structural and evolutionary information</article-title><source>Bioinformatics</source><year>2005</year><volume>21</volume><fpage>2185</fpage><lpage>2190</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15746281</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1093/bioinformatics/bti365</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Greenblatt</surname><given-names>MS</given-names></name><name><surname>Beaudet</surname><given-names>JG</given-names></name><name><surname>Gump</surname><given-names>JR</given-names></name><name><surname>Godin</surname><given-names>KS</given-names></name><name><surname>Trombley</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Koh</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Bond</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Detailed computational study of p53 and p16: using evolutionary sequence analysis and disease-associated mutations to predict the functional consequences of allelic variants</article-title><source>Oncogene</source><year>2003</year><volume>22</volume><fpage>1150</fpage><lpage>1163</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12606942</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1038/sj.onc.1206101</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tavtigian</surname><given-names>SV</given-names></name><name><surname>Deffenbaugh</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>Yin</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Judkins</surname><given-names>T</given-names><